# Auth & Data Access

All authentication is handled by [Clerk](https://clerk.com/). Users must only ever be able to read or mutate their own data.

## Getting the Current User

In Server Components and Route Handlers, use Clerk's `auth()` helper. Always guard against unauthenticated access.

```ts
import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server";

const { userId } = await auth();
if (!userId) {
  // redirect or return 401
}
```

## Scoping Database Queries

Every query that touches user-owned data **must** filter by `clerkUserId`. Never fetch a row by `id` alone without also asserting ownership.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — ownership enforced
const deck = await db
  .select()
  .from(decksTable)
  .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.clerkUserId, userId)))
  .then((rows) => rows[0]);

// ❌ BAD — any user can fetch any deck by id
const deck = await db
  .select()
  .from(decksTable)
  .where(eq(decksTable.id, deckId))
  .then((rows) => rows[0]);
```

## Mutations

For `update` and `delete`, always include `clerkUserId` in the `where` clause so a user cannot modify another user's rows even if they guess an id.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
await db
  .update(decksTable)
  .set({ name })
  .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.clerkUserId, userId)));

await db
  .delete(decksTable)
  .where(and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.clerkUserId, userId)));
```

## Indirect Ownership (cards)

`cardsTable` has no `clerkUserId` — ownership is asserted through the parent deck. Before operating on a card, verify the parent deck belongs to the current user.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — verify deck ownership before touching its cards
const deck = await db.query.decksTable.findFirst({
  where: and(eq(decksTable.id, deckId), eq(decksTable.clerkUserId, userId)),
});
if (!deck) throw new Error("Not found");

await db.delete(cardsTable).where(eq(cardsTable.id, cardId));
```

## Inserts

Always stamp new rows with the current user's `clerkUserId`.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
await db.insert(decksTable).values({ clerkUserId: userId, name, description });
```
